# Intent: Safety fix, train 1. One shared millisecond-stamp helper (maipai_time_core.h) and its uses: hold, quiet, grace and lockout windows that never ended after 24.9 days of uptime. Lock tools: an attempt limit, a current code to turn the auto lock off, and the three tools hidden from the model. Remote gate: the locked rule no longer depends on the caller's own source word, and a running session keeps its first host id. Pickup: a lift while the unit moves its own head is detected.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: self.lock.set with a wrong current five times answers too_many; self.lock.config auto_minutes 0 with no current answers current_needed; lifting the unit by hand and tilting it past 70 degrees while it dances stops the dance within about two seconds.
# Kconfig: none

